# The function escapes, so it has two ways in. A caller that nobody knows comes in with any values: each is tested, an integer is converted and a double unboxed, and the result is boxed.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="area" role=EntryChecks
# CHECK: AboveEqual(
# CHECK: IToD(
# CHECK: AboveEqual(
# CHECK: IToD(
# CHECK: Double b@[[checkedArea]] = Mul(
# CHECK: Return(
# What is no number leaves by a jump to the copy that takes any value.
# CHECK: Void b@{{*}} = Patchpoint(b@{{*}}:Register({{*}}), b@{{*}}:Register({{*}}), runsWithoutFrame, resultConstraints = WarmAny, Terminal|{{*}}:CallDirect)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# The typed body takes two floating-point registers and tests nothing.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="area" role=Source
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#0:
# CHECK-NEXT: Double b@[[width]] = ArgumentReg(
# CHECK-NEXT: Double b@[[height]] = ArgumentReg(
# CHECK-NEXT: Double b@[[area]] = Mul(b@[[width]], b@[[height]],
# CHECK-NEXT: Return(b@[[area]], Terminal)
# CHECK-NEXT: end of function
# A caller whose arguments are proven to be numbers calls the typed body.
